# Copy to .claude/sensitive-patterns.local (untracked) and list names of
# your private Polarion deployment (project/space/document ids) that must
# never appear in PR/issue/commit/release text.
#
# One Python regex per line, case-sensitive — prefix `(?i)` to also catch
# lowercased variants (URL slugs etc.); `#` = comment; invalid regex
# guarded as literal. Enforced by .claude/hooks/block_sensitive_text.py
# on outward commands (gh pr/issue/api/release/gist/repo/label/workflow,
# git commit/tag/push — push catch private names in branch names).
#
# Untracked = absent in fresh worktree checkouts. Claude sessions started
# inside a worktree auto-link it from the main checkout
# (link_sensitive_patterns.py SessionStart hook); outside Claude, copy or
# symlink the .local file into each worktree you publish from.
#
# ExamplePrivateProject\b
# (?i)examplespace/exampleprivatedoc\b
